# CVE-2026-12151: undici DoS via unbounded WebSocket memory growth.
# Affected package: undici bundled inside npm's own node_modules, not in application code.
# npm is used only as a process runner (CMD ["npm", "start"]), not as an HTTP/WebSocket client.
# Exploitability: negligible — npm never opens a WebSocket in this deployment context.
CVE-2026-12151

# GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj (CVE-2026-33327, CVE-2026-33328, CVE-2026-35590, CVE-2026-35591)
# libvips vulnerabilities inherited by sharp, bundled as an optionalDependency of next@16.2.x.
# next@16.2.x pins sharp@^0.34.5 — npm overrides do not apply to optionalDependencies and
# no updated Next.js release is available. sharp is used for static image optimisation only
# (not processing user-supplied data), so the attack surface is minimal.
GHSA-f88m-g3jw-g9cj
CVE-2026-33327
CVE-2026-33328
CVE-2026-35590
CVE-2026-35591
